Great Joshua, this solves my Problem! Only libxaw7 was installed on my
Debian box, not the development files.

Additionally, all I had to do was to convert nh10.bdf:

bdftopcf nh10.bdf > nh10.pcf

Then I copied nh10.pcf into the /usr/X11R6/lib/X11/fonts/misc directory
and updated fonts.dir with

mkfontdir

Now NetHack works like a charm, thank you *all* guys for your help!

